title The replay that was a merge
prompt Bakery lane, autonomous lap: the most durable still-solvable work in core infrastructure.
rota lap 5123, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; read up close and run the actual thing. It is why I ran the control against the new binary before trusting the stash's own GREEN, and why I read the pin's byte count rather than assuming a recovered row fits.
think The round-open named it: one session log in the dead-letter box and nowhere else. stash@{0} held a whole finished lap of this ship -- the key_wanted repair, 294 insertions across 11 files, its account, its row, its log -- stashed at 195406, one minute before this lap opened. The card's own MINE line named that repair as the lane's crux.
think Its base was 4af8235dfe and HEAD stood seven commits past it. A replay is a merge, so I read what the merge could not know rather than trusting the diff.
think Conflict one, the ledger head: my row booked %779 and the anointed spine had bound that view to a peer's awk-generator row inside the same hour. Rebased to %780 off the spine's own --next; the stamp 20260916.193716 never moved, which is rule 4's whole point.
think Conflict two, the fold recital: my lap folded %769 and %773 together and a peer had since folded %773 alone. Keeping both would have stood %773 in two files, which reds the monotone guard. Dropped my shelf whole and kept upstream's fold; %769 stays on the pin where upstream keeps it.
think Then the reading no replay could have carried: the recovered row took the pin to 67,802 against a bound of 65,536. At HEAD it read 64,648, so my own row is what crossed it -- the ledger was at capacity and my arrival is what said so.
think Folded %777 and %779 rather than shortening the row, which is the cure the pin's own header names. They teach one thing together: a reference in this tree carries two promises, and only the mechanical half had an instrument -- %777 a citation whose path was guarded and whose section was not, %779 a comment promising reproducibility and variety in one word where only the first could be checked.
think Building refused with FileBusy: a cadence-slice roster pass from the dead lap still held rye/bin/rye, 19 minutes in and in THIS tree. Resolved its cwd through /proc rather than reaching for a pattern, left it running, emitted to rye/bin/rye.new and ran the control against that path -- the control takes a binary argument for exactly this.
obs The stash's own GREEN proved nothing here. Seven commits had landed under it, so I re-ran the control on metal at this HEAD before the binary moved into place: 25 legs, every flip missing and every hit holding.
obs Three of the four conflicts were invisible in the diff. A renumber, a superseded fold, and a byte bound are all facts about the tree the stash landed INTO, and a replay reads only the tree it left.
obs Left the cold roster pass running rather than signaling it. It will read tree_moved, honestly, because the tree did move under it -- and a pass whose reading is muddied is cheaper than a pass killed by a hand that wanted its binary back.
loom rye_run_warm_ms=45 rye_run_warm_ms=48 ryekey_legs=25 ryekey_control_s=120
loom reds_pin_before=67802 reds_pin_after=57777 reds_pin_bound=65536 rows_folded=2
file rye/src/main.rye recovered whole -- the cheap four move ahead of the read as key_wanted, RYE_BUILD_FRESH gains its own refusal sentence
file tools/fixtures/r/ryekey_control.sh legs 20, 21 and 22 recovered; 25 proven on metal at this HEAD
file tools/r/ryekey_witness.rish its summary reads twenty-five, and the control answered green beneath it
file construction/REDS.md row %780, rebased off the anointed spine from the %779 the stash booked; %777 and %779 folded to bring the pin under its bound
file construction/archive/REDS-a-reference-makes-two-promises-and-one-of-them-had-a-guard-rows-777-779.md the shelf head, graded A+/98 at Meter
file construction/ITINERARY.md the recovered account plus what the replay could not copy, stamp refreshed
scope recover one dead lap whole against a moved HEAD: rebase its row, drop its superseded fold, fold the ledger under its bound, and re-prove the repair on metal
status GREEN -- ryekey 25 legs, reds-pin-capacity, reds-monotone, tracked-link, link-text-promise, unshared-citation, ascii-comment, ascii-document, width-check and tame_style_check all green on metal; the cold roster pass this lap inherited is still in flight and its tree moved under it
recommend keep-going -- the hit path still hashes 172MB to answer a question inode, size, mtime and ctime settle, and that memo is the lane's next crux
